Isoline
=======

Isoline is a fork of OpenCNCPilot by Martin Pittermann (martin2250),
https://github.com/martin2250/OpenCNCPilot, used under the MIT License.
The original copyright notice is preserved in LICENSE, and the upstream commit
history is preserved in this repository's git history.

What Isoline changes
--------------------

* Split into Isoline.Core (platform independent G-code, height map, Gerber and
  toolpath code) and Isoline.App (the WPF shell), with a unit test suite.
* Migrated from .NET Framework 4.6 to .NET 8.
* Reads Gerber files and generates isolation toolpaths directly, removing the
  round trip through external CAM software.
* Rebuilt user interface: token based theming, always-visible digital readout,
  keyboard jogging, decoded alarms, job progress and time estimation.
* Bicubic height map interpolation and probe outlier rejection.
* Job recovery after an alarm or lost connection.
* Machine calibration (steps/mm) read/write and a measurement wizard.
* Support for grblHAL and FluidNC alongside Grbl and uCNC.

Third party components
----------------------

Clipper2                 Boost Software License 1.0   https://github.com/AngusJohnson/Clipper2
HelixToolkit.Wpf         MIT License                  https://github.com/helix-toolkit/helix-toolkit
System.IO.Ports          MIT License                  https://github.com/dotnet/runtime
xUnit.net                Apache License 2.0           https://github.com/xunit/xunit

The Grbl and uCNC error, alarm and setting code tables in
src/Isoline.App/Resources are derived from the Grbl and uCNC projects.

The expression evaluator in src/Isoline.Core/Expressions replaces the
martin2250.Calculator package that upstream depended on; it is an original
implementation written for this fork so that the core could target .NET 8.
